WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.036
Well, today, we're learning

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.037
that President Biden's

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:04.804
legal team

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.706
found another batch

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:07.941
of classified documents.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:08.274
A source

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.610
saying these documents came in searches

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.413
that began after the November discovery

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.849
of the classified dogs from president.

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:16.549
Now, President

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.318
Biden's time as vice president

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:20.320
and an old office in Washington, D.C.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.621
So the question really is

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.656
what does this mean for the president?

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.191
How are we just now learning about this

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.360
and also the DOJ going forward?

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.396
Joining me now, CNN special correspondent

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.530
Jamie Gangel,

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.731
CNN senior law enforcement

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.500
analyst Andrew McCabe, and CNN

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.568
legal analyst Elliot Williams.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:36.603
I'm glad you're all here.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.003
And I bet

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.905
we have similar questions

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.407
as to who, what, when,

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.242
the question of who knew what, when, why.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:43.443
But I want to begin with you, Jamie,

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.945
because there is we don't know.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.380
Well, there we go to that

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.615
end of the segment today.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.316
Thank you for watching CNN.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.251
No, seriously.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:51.818
I mean, I'm

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:52.919
trying to wrap my mind

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.020
around some of the reporting

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.822
that's come in over the last 24 hours,

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.891
even in a statement in Mexico City.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.093
And there were about 40 boxes

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.061
that were handed over.

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.395
And an abundance of caution

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.631
from the first batch we learned about

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:05.432
it doesn't necessarily

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:07.767
add up to ten classified docs or not

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.669
whatever level they were.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.371
But are these new batch?

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.173
Is this from a different location

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.308
or is that part of those 40 boxes

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.709
that was handed over

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.545
a different location?

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.180
And let's just call it

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.283
an undisclosed location at the moment.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.252
The first location was his office,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.455
part of the Biden Pen Center

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:29.722
that had been sitting there

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.391
for several years.

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:33.293
These boxes were locked up.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:36.096
My understanding is 99% of

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.198
what was in that office was personal.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.633
It included things like

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.902
the burial arrangement documents

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:43.903
for Beau Biden's

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:47.040
funeral boxes of condolence letters

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.274
that had been sent to him

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:49.809
as vice president.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.678
And that's why his personal lawyer

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:52.612
was going through it,

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:54.781
because they thought it was all personal

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.216
and confidential.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.651
And then that lawyer gets to a box.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.220
He opens it up.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.756
There's a folder marked VIP, personal,

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.692
not unimportant.

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:06.726
He opens that up.

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.261
It says Classified

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:10.063
He closes it again

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:12.098
and he calls the White House counsel.

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.867
He says, Houston, we have a problem.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.902
They say, call the National Archives

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:18.571
And that first

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:19.105
batch, there

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:21.341
were about four boxes that they found

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.543
that seemed to be different

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:26.913
from all the other 36 personal boxes.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.748
And those had both

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.917
those ten classified documents

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:33.153
and then other documents

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.721
that were unclassified.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:35.522
But fall under

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.223
the Presidential Records Act,

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.791
Sorry for the long explanation.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:39.993
So it is out to me

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.961
here because it sounds like one

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.663
there's different locations, Andrew,

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.331
where things are, but also

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.666
and an abundance of caution to

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.834
then just say, here

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:48.902
you go, here's the whole kit

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.069
and caboodle.

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.437
Of course, the issue

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:54.607
and there are many issues here

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.076
is are people giving

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.111
President Biden

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:01.548
a pass on the idea of work this happened?

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:02.715
This is not the response

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.150
people had for the former

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.318
president Donald Trump.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.553
Of course, the big distinction here

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:08.488
is how one behaved

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.356
once they were aware of it.

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.292
Is that a distinction that you think

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.927
should be highlighted more

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.130
It's a very significant distinction,

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.198
and particularly

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:19.999
in the context of the investigation

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.000
that will follow.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.602
So is he getting a pass?

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:23.770
No, I don't believe he's

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.571
going to get a pass.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.105
He's going to be investigated.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.141
And I would opine likely

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.542
by a special counsel.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.343
He's already better U.S.

00:03:30.343 --> 00:03:31.377
attorney out of Illinois,

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:34.113
a Trump appointee. That's right.

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.181
And at this point,

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.249
I think the attorney general

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:36.616
would be

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:37.550
well advised

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:37.984
to appoint

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:38.851
a special counsel

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.020
over this investigation of how

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:43.223
President Biden and his team handled

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.157
these documents.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.259
That's a separate issue.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:49.495
But I think his the distinctions

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:50.730
between how his

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.532
he and his team have handled this

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:53.600
and how President Trump

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.167
and his lawyers

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.301
handled the situation tomorrow

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.037
could not be more distinct. Right.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.906
It's it's it's night and day.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.741
It's an overabundance of caution.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.711
Contacting the archives immediately,

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:05.545
having them

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:06.713
come out the next day

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.281
to recover all of the documents.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:08.815
There's no

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:09.716
parsing of, well,

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:10.583
you can look in this room

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.417
and not in that room

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.752
where you can look in the doorway

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:13.920
but not go in the boxes.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.421
They handed everything over.

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.390
I think following in that caution,

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.759
they are now searching other locations

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.561
where documents could maybe

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:23.630
have ended up as well.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.031
Contrast that to what's happening

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.833
right now in the Mar a Lago case.

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.401
You have the Department of Justice

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:30.003
fighting it out with Trump's

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.204
lawyers in court

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:33.273
to try to hold them in contempt

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:34.974
for failing to do exactly

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:36.476
what the Biden team is doing right now.

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:37.343
That is going out

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.845
and searching other locations.

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:39.545
You have the Trump

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.480
team refusing

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.948
to turn over the names

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.950
of the two private investigators

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.151
they hired to go out

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.419
and do their own search,

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:47.987
refusing to turn over the names

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:48.921
of those investigators

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.023
because they basically don't

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.658
want the department to know who they are.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:53.259
So Very different reaction.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.494
There is a cooperation on it.

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:55.628
So it's an important issue here.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.530
But just for the audience,

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:00.033
that is it, all this, all that common.

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.234
We're hearing about it in real time

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:03.136
and so several months about this.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.804
But the fact that there is,

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:05.505
you know, in the law,

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:07.006
we think about custodian of records

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.408
and chain of custody.

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:10.009
Is there really no one out there

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:12.445
who is realizing that they're missing

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.314
some of these top secret documents?

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:15.815
How is this continuously happening?

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:17.283
Yeah, I think the big picture point is

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:18.251
that we just need

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:18.951
a better system

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:20.253
of the United States of tracking

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.088
what happens with classified information

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:23.122
after the turn up,

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.490
not just a presidential administration,

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.526
but after people leave government.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:26.826
Right.

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:27.627
So aside,

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:28.695
that's the big picture thing

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:30.129
that affects both of these presidents.

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:31.431
Now, as of this question, it's

00:05:31.431 --> 00:05:32.231
a really important one.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.399
The floor about

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:34.967
is a pass being given

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.002
to one party or another.

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.670
And it's really important to focus on,

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:37.970
at least

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.305
with former President Trump,

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:41.541
a federal judge had found

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:43.076
that there was probable cause

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:43.443
to believe

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:44.310
that there would be evidence

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.278
of a series of crimes,

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:46.012
including, number one,

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.347
obstruction of justice,

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:50.650
no to removal or mutilation of documents.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:51.250
And, three,

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.952
mishandling of defense information.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:54.287
And then beyond that,

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:55.455
there was the open question

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:56.556
of the amount of time,

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:57.924
the staggering amount of time over

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:58.691
several months

00:05:58.691 --> 00:05:59.792
where the former president

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.861
and with the aid of his lawyers

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:02.395
was help

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:04.664
was allegedly frustrating

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.265
the department's investigation.

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:07.400
You mean the search warrant,

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.002
probable cause to certify Lago?

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.304
Yeah, outlined all of this.

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.873
And so it's just apples and oranges here.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:14.407
Now, look,

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:15.775
we may find that

00:06:15.775 --> 00:06:17.777
President Biden and his attorneys

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:19.412
are thwarting the investigation

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:20.413
of the Justice Department,

00:06:20.413 --> 00:06:22.348
but that's simply not the case right now.

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:23.916
And if that evidence were to emerge,

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.351
of course, the president

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:26.085
the current president

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:26.819
should be investigated.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:27.820
But that's just not the case.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.856
And I think this desire to make it

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.924
one side versus the other thing,

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.693
you just can't do that to every case.

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:34.861
And it's just not not the case here.

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:36.429
We are a society that draws

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.830
distinctions, analogies

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:38.731
probably more often

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:39.499
than we should

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:40.700
However,

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.101
there were a lot of questions today,

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:42.635
and here

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:43.770
just a couple of them

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:44.570
that were asked

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.672
and of the White House press secretary,

00:06:46.672 --> 00:06:47.807
Cohen Jean-Pierre,

00:06:47.807 --> 00:06:49.242
that she declined to answer

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:51.244
who brought the documents to the office?

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:53.146
Did Biden himself bring them?

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:54.914
Why did it take so long to disclose

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:55.882
discovery of the public?

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:56.549
Was a timing

00:06:56.549 --> 00:06:58.451
related to the midterm elections?

00:06:58.451 --> 00:06:59.786
Were there any other things found?

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:01.087
Is there an audit underway?

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:02.522
Was he briefed? When was he briefed?

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:04.223
Why were the private lawyers doing this?

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:05.291
A number of questions

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:06.392
that she declined to answer

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:07.293
because she cited

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:09.295
an ongoing investigation

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:10.797
But that election part,

00:07:10.797 --> 00:07:12.799
the when the people are finding out

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:14.400
that is going to be

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.302
something that already has legs

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:19.105
and might continue to run as he intends

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:21.240
to run for the reelection campaign.

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:22.308
Do you have a sense

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:23.142
as to why

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:24.811
they haven't gotten out ahead of this?

00:07:24.811 --> 00:07:27.013
I mean, from Monday to now?

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:29.182
Why not just say more?

00:07:29.816 --> 00:07:32.485
I think the issue of why wait so long

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:33.619
is a real issue

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:34.287
that's going to have

00:07:34.287 --> 00:07:36.756
political consequences for him.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:38.958
People don't like to hear this,

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:41.260
but this is a gift to Donald Trump

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.328
and the Republicans.

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:45.665
And waiting so long is part of that gift.

00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:47.200
That said,

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.068
maybe their reasoning is

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:50.736
that they were cooperating

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:51.871
with an investigation.

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:52.305
I don't know.

00:07:52.305 --> 00:07:55.241
But the political fallout is what it is.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:56.642
I will say,

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.744
I don't think there's much of a chance

00:07:58.744 --> 00:07:59.612
that Joe Biden

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:03.549
Kerry did these, you know, 40 boxes here.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:05.418
I have a

00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:06.619
source who is very familiar

00:08:06.619 --> 00:08:08.521
with the documents for the record.

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:11.224
He is a lifelong registered Republican,

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:12.291
and he knows a lot

00:08:12.291 --> 00:08:14.460
about how these things are handled

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.361
over the years.

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:16.229
He thinks

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:18.798
it was very likely an honest mistake.

00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:21.601
The real question today is,

00:08:21.601 --> 00:08:22.535
what are these

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:24.237
other new documents

00:08:24.237 --> 00:08:25.771
that were found in these?

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:26.873
Your eyebrow raised

00:08:26.873 --> 00:08:27.974
the thought of an honest mistake.

00:08:27.974 --> 00:08:29.075
Maybe the FBI within you

00:08:29.075 --> 00:08:30.343
was an honest mistake.

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:32.111
What did you say about an honest mistake?

00:08:32.111 --> 00:08:32.612
Go ahead.

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:33.579
Yes, actually.

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:35.448
And Eliot can back me up on this.

00:08:35.448 --> 00:08:36.782
These sort of referrals

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:38.251
from the National Archives

00:08:38.251 --> 00:08:39.819
or other places about the concerns

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:41.187
about classified documents

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:43.322
that may be outside of the facilities.

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:45.091
They come to the department

00:08:45.091 --> 00:08:47.193
and to the FBI all the time.

00:08:47.193 --> 00:08:48.961
And most of them are resolved

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.763
without criminal charges.

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:53.633
The bureau's first concern is to find out

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.568
where is this stuff, let's get it back

00:08:55.568 --> 00:08:56.969
and to conduct an assessment

00:08:56.969 --> 00:08:57.570
as to whether or not

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:59.338
there's been damage to national security.

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:01.007
Have we compromised sources and methods?

00:09:01.007 --> 00:09:02.041
Do we need to move people?

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.876
Do we need to remove technologies

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:05.244
from places that they are helping

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:06.312
us collect intelligence

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:08.447
And once that's done,

00:09:08.447 --> 00:09:09.782
that's when you start thinking about

00:09:09.782 --> 00:09:10.983
could it have been an honest

00:09:10.983 --> 00:09:12.118
mistake, i.e.,

00:09:12.118 --> 00:09:13.719
do we not have enough evidence

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:15.521
to prove the intent

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:16.889
to mishandled documents

00:09:16.889 --> 00:09:19.091
that's required under those statutes?

00:09:19.091 --> 00:09:21.060
So there will be a time for all that.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.261
And all of these facts

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:22.862
that you've mentioned

00:09:22.862 --> 00:09:24.397
are going to be a joint issue

00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:25.565
where I come back to this point

00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:26.165
and it's important to hear

00:09:26.165 --> 00:09:27.033
all your perspectives.

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:27.466
And of course,

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:29.101
remember that the reason we know

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:30.937
about the search on Mar

00:09:30.937 --> 00:09:33.439
a Lago and the entire course of events

00:09:33.439 --> 00:09:34.674
between Trump

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:36.776
and the archives is because Trump

00:09:36.776 --> 00:09:37.176
was the one

00:09:37.176 --> 00:09:38.344
to have said something about it.

00:09:38.344 --> 00:09:39.478
So maybe there was a

00:09:39.478 --> 00:09:40.246
maybe a lesson

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:42.148
learned and it's gone awry. Who knows?

